---
flm:
  math: false
  use: [flmdoc]
---
A single backtick: `x`. Two backticks around a single one: ``a`b``. Three around two:
```a``b```.

One space at each end is removed: `` `a` `` holds a backtick at each end, and ` x `
holds x alone. A space at one end only is kept: ` x`. A span of spaces only is kept:
`  `.

A backslash and a percent sign are raw characters: `\emph{x} % y`, and so are braces:
`{` and `}`.

A span may be wrapped: `over
two lines`, and ``
x
`` has a line ending at each end.
